		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3708&amp;p=28959#p28959"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Thanks<br><br>Speaker clicks when playing beeps etc are also in the official firmware, so this appears to be a fault in the electronics design of this radio.<br>I will investigate whether there is anything I can do in the firmware to reduce them, perhaps using the same method of "click suppression" which I used for the MD9600, but at the moment I don't know if that will be possible on the MD2017<br><br>The supurious speaker clicks are only on DMR and occur when the Green LED illuminates / flashes occasionally when there is no DMR signal.<br>People reported the same problem on the DM-1701 but I didn't have time to test this.<br><br>BTW.<br><br>For me DMR audio is a lot quieter than FM audio, so I will investigate whether I can change the FM audio gain to reduce this imbalance</div></blockquote>Hey. Part of alpha testing is prompt feedback. Now, I haven't looked at your code, but I guess that it has - tops - some Unit testing in it, if at all, but I can't really visualize how you could do automated integration testing, and much less automated UAT. After all, that's what you have us testers for. <br><br>(I build Platforms, Cloud automation and SDLCs (CI/CD) for a living, don't know if somehow that's showing a bit)<br><br>Keep the releases coming, and rest assured that, other financially gainful workload allowing, you'll receive as prompt and detailed feedback as possible. <br><br>After all, we can't be thankful enough for all the work that you have put into OpenGD77. People often forget the amount of work that is behind widely used open-source projects and take it as a "given", when there is always people behind it.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5355">EA7KLK</a> — Thu Jan 25, 2024 2:27 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
